<title>CHINA: Cathay Pacific to cut 350 jobs - paper.</title>
<headline>Cathay Pacific to cut 350 jobs - paper.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong flag carrier Cathay Pacific Airways Ltd will cut 350 jobs but some of the affected employees may be redeployed to other parts of the group, Apple Daily newspaper said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The move is necessary because the jobs will be contracted out to service suppliers after the airline's airport-based operation moves to the new Chek Lap Kok airport from the existing Kai Tak airport, the newspaper quoted a Cathay spokeswoman as saying.</p>
<p>But the group will help affected employees to transfer to its subsidiaries and related suppliers, and offer reasonable compensation, she was quoted as saying.</p>
<p>Cathay officials were not immediately available to comment.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6590</p>
</text>
